            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "G. When the Employer uses temporary employment agency employees it will notify the Union, require the employment agency to pay the Employee the applicable contract rate of pay and require the employee to join the Union if the temporary assignment lasts longer than thirty-one (31) work days for store temporaries and three months for clerical employees. If any Agency employee assignment lasts beyond thirty-one (31) working days for store temporaries and three months for clerical temporaries, the Agency Employee must become a regular employee. Said Temporary Agency Employees will be required to follow Section 3 in regards to payment of Union dues and fees if their assignment lasts thirty-one (31) working days or more for store temporaries, and three months for clerical temporary workers. Upon request of a representative of the Union, at a mutually agreeable time the Union representative may review invoices from the Employment Agency.",
            "block_bbox": [
                347,
                740,
